# Morrowind vampirism, Clan Aundae: catching Porphyric Hemophilia and the turn, carried by Skyrim's vampirism.
# The Aundae vampires of the Dulo, Aralen and Sarethi tombs (Vampire_Aundae gives each its blood) attack a stranger
# and flee after a few blows (authored Flee 70), so the player seeks out each in turn; their hits pass on "Vampire
# Blood Aundae", which converts as Skyrim's vampire disease (10% a hit). Infecting from Dhaunayne herself would
# leave her fighting the player for good: SetFight never ends a fight (OpenMW's OpSetAiSetting). Three days on, a
# sleep in Caius Cosades' bed turns the player:
# VampireCheck starts Vampire_Aundae_PC (PCVampire 1, VampClan 1, the clan's Specials) and Skyrim's
# PlayerVampireQuest.VampireChange makes the player a Skyrim vampire. The generic Morrowind abilities are Skyrim's
# to give, so Vampire Sun Damage never lands on the player.
# Run: python -m tools.live.test_instance --instance 2 mwtest --cases <this folder> --fast --checkpoints --stop-on-fail --load mwtest_a1_11_report --timeout 3600
# See docs/commentary/headless_testing.md#quest-runs

case va_aundae_infect
approach 053E1E58
wait 200
approach 052D64B1
wait 200
approach 053C5D68
wait 200
approach 05826ECA
wait 200
approach 05BE5476
wait 200
approach 057AF45F
wait 200
approach 053E90AA
wait 200
approach 05DAF1FD
wait 200
approach 05588CCD
wait 200
approach 05D63F0E
wait 200
approach 05572B34
wait 200
approach 05DC6EA3
wait 200
approach 05B0B02A
wait 200
approach 0521688A
wait 200
approach 05D9E582
until 600 player->GetSpell "Vampire Blood Aundae" == 1
end

case va_aundae_turn
run
player->PositionCell -60 -30 60 0 "Balmora, Caius Cosades' House"
until 300 GetPCCell "Balmora, Caius Cosades' House" == 1
wait 60
rest 120 05201D4E PCVampire == 1
expect VampClan == 1
expect player->GetSpell "Vampire Aundae Specials" == 1
expect player->GetSpell "Vampire Sun Damage" == 0
expect player->GetSpell "Vampire Blood Aundae" == 0
end
